stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ONLINE: Admin: POST /api/v1/gates<br/>→ INSERT gates (id, …, status='ONLINE', is_active=TRUE)<br/>(auto-pinged on next cycle)

    ONLINE --> OFFLINE: Ping fails<br/>CronManager → POST /api/v1/admin/ping-gates<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='OFFLINE'

    OFFLINE --> ONLINE: Ping succeeds<br/>CronManager → POST /api/v1/admin/ping-gates<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='ONLINE',<br/>last_ping_at=NOW()

    ONLINE --> DISABLED: Admin: PUT /api/v1/gates/{id} body status='DISABLED'<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='DISABLED'<br/>(manual disable — maintenance / decommission)

    OFFLINE --> DISABLED: Admin: PUT /api/v1/gates/{id} body status='DISABLED'<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='DISABLED'

    DISABLED --> ONLINE: Admin: PUT /api/v1/gates/{id} body status='ONLINE'<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='ONLINE'<br/>AND next ping succeeds

    note left of ONLINE
        STATUS axis (ping-job-driven, gates.status):
        ONLINE — recent ping success
        OFFLINE — recent ping fail or never pinged
        DISABLED — operator manually disabled (PUT)

        IS_ACTIVE axis (operator-driven, gates.is_active):
        TRUE  — gate participates in registry / broadcasts / ping
        FALSE — operator soft-deleted (DELETE) — see lower note
    end note

    note right of ONLINE
        Latest gates row for this id has status='ONLINE' AND is_active=TRUE.
        - Included in identifier search broadcasts.
        - gateRegistry.online() returns this gate.
        - last_ping_at on the latest row is recent.
        - eDelivery or Fast HTTP calls routed here.
    end note

    note right of OFFLINE
        Latest gates row has status='OFFLINE'.
        - Excluded from broadcasts.
        - Direct GET /v1/dataset/{eu-fi01}/… → 502 GATEWAY_UNAVAILABLE.
        - Ping job continues trying every 5 min;
          if reachable, INSERTs a new ONLINE row.
    end note

    note right of DISABLED
        Latest gates row has status='DISABLED'.
        - Excluded from broadcasts AND ping job.
        - Will NOT auto-recover. Requires admin PUT to flip back.
        - Old gates rows archived nightly by CronManager (Epic 26).
    end note

    note right of [*]
        DELETE /api/v1/gates/{id} (soft-delete):
        → INSERT gates row with is_active=FALSE.
        Status axis is unchanged on this transition; the gate
        leaves the operational set entirely (registry sync,
        peer broadcast, ping sweeps all skip is_active=FALSE).
        Distinct from status='DISABLED' (operator-paused but
        still tracked) — DELETE is logical retirement.
    end note
